# nRF24 sniffs of both Platinum remotes, 2026-11-11
# Receiver: hiBCTR nRF24L01+ module (radio A, passed `test`), no 10 uF cap yet,
# on ESP32-DevKitC. Settings: ch 33 only, 2 Mbps, address E7E7E7, CRC-16,
# 5-byte payload, auto-ack off. One channel of three, so it sees about a third
# of the packets; the 556 us minimum gap is one packet per channel rotation.
#
# Remote IDs are redacted: "xx xx" = weak remote, "yy yy" = working remote.
# They are different IDs, and both remotes move the shade.
#
# "no-group state" and "?" are the firmware's labels at the time. They are
# now "wake held" (action 80) and "wake release" (action 00).
#
# Columns: time since boot, channel, packet count, payload, decode, span of the
# run, min-max gap between received packets.

# ---- Sniff 1: weak remote. Group 1 + UP, then red-mode arrow presses (not
# ---- logged individually). The 207.48 run has no tail; probably a press whose
# ---- tail was missed.
ch 33 (2433 MHz)  rate 2m  aw 3  addr(on-air) E7 E7 E7  crc 2  pl 5  filter off (runs)
199.276790 s  ch33  x2098  xx xx 20 01 A1  ID xxxx  mode 20  group 1  UP held  span 1438.0 ms  gap 556-15584 us
200.715394 s  ch33  x432   xx xx 20 01 21  ID xxxx  mode 20  group 1  UP release  span 301.9 ms  gap 90-8214 us
207.482767 s  ch33  x89    xx xx 01 00 80  ID xxxx  mode 01  group none  no-group state  span 88.4 ms  gap 557-3691 us
208.961149 s  ch33  x31    xx xx 01 00 80  ID xxxx  mode 01  group none  no-group state  span 31.5 ms  gap 561-4936 us
208.995103 s  ch33  x254   xx xx 01 00 00  ID xxxx  mode 01  group none  ?  span 316.9 ms  gap 556-9316 us
212.149122 s  ch33  x188   xx xx 01 00 80  ID xxxx  mode 01  group none  no-group state  span 171.9 ms  gap 556-5497 us
212.321549 s  ch33  x176   xx xx 01 00 00  ID xxxx  mode 01  group none  ?  span 176.9 ms  gap 556-5589 us
224.626887 s  ch33  x118   xx xx 01 00 80  ID xxxx  mode 01  group none  no-group state  span 116.9 ms  gap 556-3695 us
224.746892 s  ch33  x222   xx xx 01 00 00  ID xxxx  mode 01  group none  ?  span 227.4 ms  gap 556-3743 us
Sniff stopped. 3608 packets.

